  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade mission to Moldova for Dutch-Romanian companies based in Romania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After the Netherlands embassy in Bucharest, Romania, and Moldova organised a &#x2018;Doing Business in Moldova&#x2019; seminar for Dutch and Romanian businesses in Romania, enough interest was gauged from the participants to go on a joint trade mission to the Republic of Moldova. This mission will take place in October 2017 during the Moldova Business Week. This event is organised by MIEPO (Moldova Investment and Export Promotion Organisation). This event will provide the trade mission participants with direct access to the gathering of many local and international companies, seminars and authorities.The trade mission aims to stimulate investments or trade of Dutch companies in or with Moldova. This mission will provide jobs, money and opportunities. All crucial for strengthening the private sector in Moldova and fitting into the ambition of the Netherlands (and the EU) to build stronger ties with countries adjacent to the EU within the framework of the EU Deep and Comprehensive Free Trade Area (DCFTA), part of the Association Agreement between the EU and Moldova.</narrative>
  </description>
